  "articleSummary": "The article argues that hiring an AI engineer requires looking beyond polished demos and résumés to assess real-world judgment, especially regarding failure handling, evaluation, and cost control. It advises managers to define the specific problem first, then use structured exercises (e.g., walking through a shipped project, handling a refund timeout) to observe how candidates think about permissions, idempotency, and measurement. The tone is a practical, cautionary analysis aimed at technical leaders. A recurring metaphor is “open the hood” to inspect the system’s internals, contrasting surface-level demos with observable evidence of decision-making.",
